+### Crawfis-Max Kernel
+Uses a reduced kernel radius (1.58 instead of the standard 2.0) to provide faster renderings and bring kernel size closer to that used in raycasting [S2]. This variant provides speedups of 25% to 45% without a significant drop in quality [S2].
+
 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** The coarse rasterization stage is $O(N)$ for projection and bounding box calculation, where $N$ is the number of ellipsoids. The selection stage is $O(P \cdot K \log K)$ or $O(P \cdot K)$ depending on sorting, where $P$ is the number of pixels and $K$ is the number of candidates per pixel.
-- **Memory Complexity:** Requires storage for the candidate list and the low-resolution buffer.
 - **Performance:** Reduces computational cost by avoiding full ray tracing for all primitives, typically selecting 10% of all ellipsoids [S1, unofficial].
 - **Strengths:** Simple to implement, reduces rendering time significantly.
