 ## Background
-Kernel Selection was introduced in the context of differentiable volume rendering using Gaussian ellipsoids, specifically in the VoGE renderer [S1, unofficial]. It is part of a coarse-to-fine rendering strategy designed to efficiently render Gaussian ellipsoids by gradually reducing the number of ellipsoids that interact with viewing rays.
+Kernel Selection was introduced in the context of differentiable volume rendering using Gaussian ellipsoids, specifically in the VoGE renderer [S1, unofficial]. It serves as a pre-processing step to select a subset of ellipsoids (10% of all) for the subsequent ray tracing stage, reducing computational cost by avoiding full ray tracing for all primitives [S1, unofficial].
 
